Third-party material contained in this repository
=================================================

The repository contains no third-party binaries. It contains the following
source material that modifies or derives from other projects.

1. Mesa
   File:     native/venus/mesa-26.0.8-farm.patch
   What:     a source patch against Mesa 26.0.8 (the Venus Vulkan driver, its
             vtest backend, Android buffer import and a gralloc backend)
   Upstream: https://www.mesa3d.org
   Licence:  MIT, the licence of the Mesa files it modifies. The patch is
             distributed under that licence.

2. virglrenderer
   File:     native/venus/virglrenderer-1.2.0-farm.patch
   What:     a source patch against virglrenderer 1.2.0 (a buffer import
             command for the vtest server and a build fix)
   Upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/virgl/virglrenderer
   Licence:  MIT, the licence of virglrenderer. The patch is distributed
             under that licence.

3. redroid
   File:     native/venus/gpu_config_venus.sh
   What:     derived from the gpu_config.sh of the redroid project, with a
             "venus" mode added
   Licence:  Apache License, Version 2.0

4. v4l2loopback
   Files:    native/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback-0.15.1-farm.patch
             native/v4l2loopback/COPYING
   What:     a source patch against v4l2loopback v0.15.1 (upstream commit
             7546a42a66d856933a75c2b0896cb735e3ca00c0)
   Upstream: https://github.com/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback
   Licence:  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. The patch is a
             modification of a GPL work and is distributed under the GPL. The
             full text is in native/v4l2loopback/COPYING. Nothing else in this
             repository links against or includes this kernel module; the
             farm only loads it and talks to it through the kernel's V4L2
             interface.


Material that is not in this repository
=======================================

The following is obtained by you, from its own publisher and under its own
licence, when you build or run the software. None of it is redistributed here.

- Android images. Docker pulls them from their upstream publisher (by
  default the redroid images) when you start or build an Android.
- The sources that native/venus/build.sh downloads and builds on your
  machine: Mesa, libdrm, virglrenderer, and the Android NDK.
- The v4l2loopback source that native/v4l2loopback/build.sh downloads.
- The camera HAL. native/camera/extract_hal.sh takes it from a BlissOS image
  that you download yourself. The result stays on your machine.
- The Python packages named in pyproject.toml, installed by pip.
- The base images of the sidecar and helper images (Alpine Linux) and the
  packages installed into them at build time.
- Programs used on the host when present: Docker, adb, scrcpy, ffmpeg,
  OpenVPN and WireGuard tools inside the sidecar image.


